<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05ZP">Proposition <span data-tag="05ZP">6.3.2.11</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a simplicial set and let $W$ be a collection of edges of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then there exists an $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}[W^{-1}]$ and a diagram $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}[W^{-1}]$ which exhibits $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}[W^{-1}]$ as a localization of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ with respect to $W$. Moreover, we can arrange that the assignment $(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}},W) \mapsto ( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}[W^{-1}], F )$ is functorial and commutes with filtered colimits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollary <a data-tag="05ZL" href="/tag/05ZL">6.3.2.9</a> with Proposition <a data-tag="01BP" href="/tag/01BP">4.1.3.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
